  "text": "<p>Summer fervors slacken;</p><p>   Sumac torches dim;</p><p>There’s bronze upon the bracken;</p><p>   September has a whim </p><p>For carmine, pearl and amber</p><p>   Touches on her green; </p><p>Busy squirrels clamber;</p><p>   Restless birds convene.</p><p></p><p>Where Indian pipe still blanches, </p><p>   Where hoary lichen flakes</p><p>Forest trunks and branches,</p><p>   The golden foxglove makes</p><p>A mimic wood that tosses</p><p>   Warning to the trees,</p><p>Then droops upon the mosses,</p><p>   Heavy with bloom and bees.</p>",
